# Trailing slashes deliberately omitted on these three.
#
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY of that name and nothing else, so a
# SYMLINK named `node_modules` is not ignored and `git add -A` will commit it.
# That is not a hypothetical: linking `node_modules` into a git worktree is the
# normal way to avoid a second 350 MB install, and doing it here put six
# self-referential symlinks into a pull request.
#
# Without the slash the pattern matches a file, a symlink or a directory, which
# is what is actually wanted — none of these three names should ever be tracked
# in any form.
node_modules
dist
out
**/src/generated
*.tsbuildinfo
*.vsix
docs/superpowers/
.superpowers/
